# SvelteKit engineering anchor

**Only apply** when the active frontend package declares @sveltejs/kit. Never apply SvelteKit patterns to a Next.js/Vite-only app.

Before a substantial change, audit or fix, run:
node "$CURSOR_DEV_TOOLKIT_ROOT/scripts/frontend-preflight.mjs" --root "$FRONTEND_ROOT" --framework sveltekit

Requires tested SvelteKit 3.0.0 and documented v3 runtime/peer minimums. Failure means STOP and ask for explicit upgrade approval. Do not auto-upgrade or apply v3 conventions to v2.

On PASS, use relevant Contents sections:
$CURSOR_DEV_TOOLKIT_ROOT/skills/engineering/_standards/sveltekit-engineering-standard.md
plus the shared Frontend Core.

Hard invariants: server-only data in server load/action, request-local identity, Svelte 5 runes semantics, native forms, correct SSR/hydration; SvelteKit 3 Vite config and #lib import migration. Remote functions remain experimental and require opt-in.

Explicit workflows: /sveltekit-engineering-audit and /sveltekit-engineering-fix.
